# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows and built into a Linux container. Git's
# autocrlf stores LF and checks out CRLF, which is fine for Python but breaks
# anything the container executes directly: `docker build` copies from the
# working tree, not from git, so a CRLF shebang arrives in the image as
# `#!/bin/sh\r` and the container exits with "no such file or directory".
#
# These paths stay LF in the working tree for that reason.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf

# Everything else follows the platform default.
* text=auto
